PROBLEM: Long N-H (N0.87,N1.01A) N1 - H2 . 1.08 Ang.  
RESPONSE: The structure was refined using an Independent Atom Model (IAM) 
against dynamical 3D electron diffraction (3D ED) data. 
It is well established that in ED, X-H bond lengths tend to be slightly longer 
than those observed in conventional X-ray diffraction due to differences in 
scattering mechanisms. Additionally, further multipole model refinement 
(not included in the current CIF) leads to more accurate X-H distances.
;
